(3311487, 460808, 53316, '<td valign="top">I usually don''t care for shallow DOF.  But here I think it works.  I''m backwards I guess, ''cause I know a lot of people love shallow DOF but would think that this shot has your subject blurry / out of focus.  But I really feel that there is emphasis on the sidewalk for a reason - like the kid really is showing the way.  I do wish that the figure on the left were more in the frame but other than that I like this a bunch.</td>', 'I usually don''t care for shallow DOF.  But here I think it works.  I''m backwards I guess, ''cause I know a lot of people love shallow DOF but would think that this shot has your subject blurry / out of focus.  But I really feel that there is emphasis on the sidewalk for a reason - like the kid really is showing the way.  I do wish that the figure on the left were more in the frame but other than that I like this a bunch.', '2007-02-01 02:21:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(3311501, 449325, 53316, '<td valign="top">I like this except for the non-symetrical aspect.  Being an abstract I think it could get tilted any way you like, but I feel there is something off due to the lines lines exited the frame at different places. well, maybe I am wrong. Maybe it would make for a boring composition.  This certainly is a dynamic shot.  Okay, so I won''t be marking down for non-symmetricalness!</td>', 'I like this except for the non-symetrical aspect.  Being an abstract I think it could get tilted any way you like, but I feel there is something off due to the lines lines exited the frame at different places. well, maybe I am wrong. Maybe it would make for a boring composition.  This certainly is a dynamic shot.  Okay, so I won''t be marking down for non-symmetricalness!', '2007-02-01 02:26:30.000000', NULL, 1),
