(3316955, 447891, 67841, '<td valign="top">There''s a lot to like about this scene, but your composition fell a little short.  The centering doesn''t work well here - this would have been a good candidate for applying the rule of thirds.  Your horizon appears off as well - but again, the centering only accentuates that.  Your reds are gorgeous, but I would have pulled more blues out in post to really give it some punch. <br/> <br/>It''s not a bad photo by any means, but it really could have been a great one with the application of a little theory!  I, for one, am someone who regularly fails to compose a scene to it''s greatest potential so perhaps I''m punishing the artist for the sins of the viewer...  Good luck!   &lt;&lt; 7 &gt;&gt;</td>', 'There''s a lot to like about this scene, but your composition fell a little short.  The centering doesn''t work well here - this would have been a good candidate for applying the rule of thirds.  Your horizon appears off as well - but again, the centering only accentuates that.  Your reds are gorgeous, but I would have pulled more blues out in post to really give it some punch.  It''s not a bad photo by any means, but it really could have been a great one with the application of a little theory!  I, for one, am someone who regularly fails to compose a scene to it''s greatest potential so perhaps I''m punishing the artist for the sins of the viewer...  Good luck!   << 7 >>', '2007-02-02 00:44:28.000000', NULL, 1),
