(3344346, 454638, 65438, '<td valign="top">I actually like the grainy look to the photo.  It works well with the B&amp;W.</td>', 'I actually like the grainy look to the photo.  It works well with the B&W.', '2007-02-08 13:18:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344377, 457487, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals:  Well done.  You did a good job managing the sun directly in the shot.  We have nice gradient in the sky instead of vast amounts of blow out.<br/> <br/>The feel: I think the composition hurts here.  I do like the clouds as an addition and would keep them, but I would have moved so the tail fills up more completely the frame (that is, less negative space in the direction of the sun).  Personally, I don''t like the speedwing detail.  I like to have objects either have a good dynamic range of detail or be compeltely sillouetted.  This is sort of a quasi-world in between and that usually fails.<br/> <br/>The game: Yes, a subtle shot for DPC.  Don''t worry about the score on a shot like this.  However, I do think you could have made some improvements (as mentioned above).</td>', 'The technicals:  Well done.  You did a good job managing the sun directly in the shot.  We have nice gradient in the sky instead of vast amounts of blow out. The feel: I think the composition hurts here.  I do like the clouds as an addition and would keep them, but I would have moved so the tail fills up more completely the frame (that is, less negative space in the direction of the sun).  Personally, I don''t like the speedwing detail.  I like to have objects either have a good dynamic range of detail or be compeltely sillouetted.  This is sort of a quasi-world in between and that usually fails. The game: Yes, a subtle shot for DPC.  Don''t worry about the score on a shot like this.  However, I do think you could have made some improvements (as mentioned above).', '2007-02-08 13:23:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344386, 454883, 24454, '<td valign="top">Judy, this is AWESOME!  I missed seeing this one!  I might have thought those textured hands were Philup''s :)   Amazing character in this!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Judy, this is AWESOME!  I missed seeing this one!  I might have thought those textured hands were Philup''s :)   Amazing character in this!! ', '2007-02-08 13:25:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344397, 456469, 8891, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon, Judy!  Way long overdue. Hurray!!!</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon, Judy!  Way long overdue. Hurray!!!', '2007-02-08 13:26:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344408, 459601, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals: lighting is good. colors are nicely contrasted.  Yes, it''s sharp.  You get away with it on the guitar on my monitor, but I run 1900x1200 and I bet on a lower res it is too sharp.  The sharpness, however, does not work with the texture of your wall.  It comes across as noise.  I would have applied a gaussian blur to the background (or just masked off the sharpening).  Is the guitar slanting just slightly to the left?<br/> <br/>The feel: A nice feel and a simple shot.  I mostly like the contrast of the blues and orange and the curve of the body.<br/> <br/>The game: A subtle shot.  If you enter subtle, don''t worry about the score not being in the stratosphere.  It rarely happens on DPC.</td>', 'The technicals: lighting is good. colors are nicely contrasted.  Yes, it''s sharp.  You get away with it on the guitar on my monitor, but I run 1900x1200 and I bet on a lower res it is too sharp.  The sharpness, however, does not work with the texture of your wall.  It comes across as noise.  I would have applied a gaussian blur to the background (or just masked off the sharpening).  Is the guitar slanting just slightly to the left? The feel: A nice feel and a simple shot.  I mostly like the contrast of the blues and orange and the curve of the body. The game: A subtle shot.  If you enter subtle, don''t worry about the score not being in the stratosphere.  It rarely happens on DPC.', '2007-02-08 13:28:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344481, 459264, 47316, '<td valign="top">Aaww this is really nice!</td>', 'Aaww this is really nice!', '2007-02-08 13:55:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344505, 458955, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals: Hmm, we could go a few ways here.  The gutsy way is to lowers the contrast on the picture on purpose to juxtapose with the name "Gray".  If you did that, I would have almost overdone it to make the intent obvious.  Otherwise, I would have added more contrast to the picture.  You are in the middle.  My guess is that it involves your conversion technique to B&amp;W.  Have you learned how to do it with the channel mixer?  This is probably one of the best methods and is far superior to "convert to grayscale".<br/> <br/>The feel: this is a nicely composed shot.  I like the quiet feel of the picture.  The only possible improvement would be to shoot at a different time to try to get some detail from the sky.  It''s either completely blown or was a completely overcast day.<br/> <br/>The game: I bet a bit more processing on the shot would have taken this from the 5.3 range to the 5.7-5.8 range.</td>', 'The technicals: Hmm, we could go a few ways here.  The gutsy way is to lowers the contrast on the picture on purpose to juxtapose with the name "Gray".  If you did that, I would have almost overdone it to make the intent obvious.  Otherwise, I would have added more contrast to the picture.  You are in the middle.  My guess is that it involves your conversion technique to B&W.  Have you learned how to do it with the channel mixer?  This is probably one of the best methods and is far superior to "convert to grayscale". The feel: this is a nicely composed shot.  I like the quiet feel of the picture.  The only possible improvement would be to shoot at a different time to try to get some detail from the sky.  It''s either completely blown or was a completely overcast day. The game: I bet a bit more processing on the shot would have taken this from the 5.3 range to the 5.7-5.8 range.', '2007-02-08 14:04:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344567, 456469, 37961, '<td valign="top">Way to Go Jo!!!!! Congrats on your first ribbon. So proud of you!</td>', 'Way to Go Jo!!!!! Congrats on your first ribbon. So proud of you!', '2007-02-08 14:20:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344570, 459264, 19708, '<td valign="top">Hey Shannon,<br/>Shame this didn''t make it to 6, as it is quite unique.<br/>I''ve seen a lot of your shots I know would have done better, but this is YOUR best, which says a lot about your free spirit and what moves you.<br/>Keep on doing what you do - it''s you, and that''s what makes it work.</td>', 'Hey Shannon,Shame this didn''t make it to 6, as it is quite unique.I''ve seen a lot of your shots I know would have done better, but this is YOUR best, which says a lot about your free spirit and what moves you.Keep on doing what you do - it''s you, and that''s what makes it work.', '2007-02-08 14:21:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344600, 461577, 66515, '<td valign="top">I was out trying to get some good shots with my red filter that I was going to convert to black and white later on. When I saw this on my screen I thought it looked great as is. If I get a chance I''ll link to the full size version which I think does this more justice.<br/> <br/>EXIF Info in the information above. You''ll note that I went -3 on the exposure compensation. It seems to help when I am using my red filter otherwise it seems to over expose a lot. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-02-08 14:34:25.</i></td>', 'I was out trying to get some good shots with my red filter that I was going to convert to black and white later on. When I saw this on my screen I thought it looked great as is. If I get a chance I''ll link to the full size version which I think does this more justice. EXIF Info in the information above. You''ll note that I went -3 on the exposure compensation. It seems to help when I am using my red filter otherwise it seems to over expose a lot. ', '2007-02-08 14:30:49.000000', '2007-02-08 14:34:25.000000', 0),
(3344651, 456469, 34659, '<td valign="top">WTG Judy!!!  Congratulations on a terrific shot and your first ribbon!  Well done.  :-D</td>', 'WTG Judy!!!  Congratulations on a terrific shot and your first ribbon!  Well done.  :-D', '2007-02-08 14:39:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344659, 461850, 56539, '<td valign="top">Don''t blame me.  I voted the other 10!</td>', 'Don''t blame me.  I voted the other 10!', '2007-02-08 14:40:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344677, 459264, 70375, '<td valign="top">Really very very very very beautiful, creative, and colourful!</td>', 'Really very very very very beautiful, creative, and colourful!', '2007-02-08 14:44:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344869, 461532, 57229, '<td valign="top">I could have done without the logo, but hey...<br/> <br/>Trying to think about why this should score so low.<br/> <br/>It''s not frighteningly original, maybe, which would be a reason not to score high, but low?<br/> <br/>Too many good shots in the challenge is always a problem (people are so inconsiderate, sometimes).<br/> <br/>The fingers and fingernails probably needed to be sharper for the voting crew around here.<br/> <br/>Shame - the denim itself comes out really well. Keep yourself a good copy and be content with that. I think most of all you fell foul of the pin-sharp convention.</td>', 'I could have done without the logo, but hey... Trying to think about why this should score so low. It''s not frighteningly original, maybe, which would be a reason not to score high, but low? Too many good shots in the challenge is always a problem (people are so inconsiderate, sometimes). The fingers and fingernails probably needed to be sharper for the voting crew around here. Shame - the denim itself comes out really well. Keep yourself a good copy and be content with that. I think most of all you fell foul of the pin-sharp convention.', '2007-02-08 15:41:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344892, 460248, 25433, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and votes guys! Very happy with top 10 finish!</td>', 'Thanks for the comments and votes guys! Very happy with top 10 finish!', '2007-02-08 15:46:01.000000', NULL, 0),
