(3353616, 452572, 49865, '<td valign="top">I am impressed with the warmth of this photo and the quality of the silhouettes. I agree with many others who have commented that it''s hard to get tired of these photos - majestic animals that are incredibly photogenic. <br/> <br/>Only two qualms with the photo: the first is the vertical cropping seems oh-so-slightly harsh. I would''ve liked a deeper vertical dimension. The other complaint is a bit more trivial - the title doesn''t really seem to fit as the two look more like they''re grazing in each other''s proximity than duking it out. <br/> <br/>Altogether a great shot and I look forward to more of your future wildlife photography efforts.</td>', 'I am impressed with the warmth of this photo and the quality of the silhouettes. I agree with many others who have commented that it''s hard to get tired of these photos - majestic animals that are incredibly photogenic.  Only two qualms with the photo: the first is the vertical cropping seems oh-so-slightly harsh. I would''ve liked a deeper vertical dimension. The other complaint is a bit more trivial - the title doesn''t really seem to fit as the two look more like they''re grazing in each other''s proximity than duking it out.  Altogether a great shot and I look forward to more of your future wildlife photography efforts.', '2007-02-11 16:46:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3353820, 457540, 72581, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SandyP:</b></div><hr/><i> Daisy, this is GORGEOUS!  So simple, yet so elegand and beautiful.  I think your second entry is just awesome!  :)   I look forward to seeing many more :)<br/> <br/>Although. . .I do wish it had been your commenters who decided your final score :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!</td>', 'Originally posted by SandyP: Daisy, this is GORGEOUS!  So simple, yet so elegand and beautiful.  I think your second entry is just awesome!  :)   I look forward to seeing many more :) Although. . .I do wish it had been your commenters who decided your final score :)   Thanks!', '2007-02-11 17:38:48.000000', NULL, 0),
