(3355491, 456495, 60862, '<td valign="top">I really like the placement of the parrot in the frame and the interesting shapes of the various leaves.  Backlit action shots are pretty tough, though.  As for the border, I thought it was the wall around a window! :)</td>', 'I really like the placement of the parrot in the frame and the interesting shapes of the various leaves.  Backlit action shots are pretty tough, though.  As for the border, I thought it was the wall around a window! :)', '2007-02-12 01:31:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3355737, 461875, 65522, '<td valign="top">Awesome picture.  The composition is right on.  There looks to be a great balance between the darks and the lights.  The reflection really adds to the symmetry of the picture, but still allows you to maintain the main subject in the left 2/3 of the picture.  Beautiful picture.</td>', 'Awesome picture.  The composition is right on.  There looks to be a great balance between the darks and the lights.  The reflection really adds to the symmetry of the picture, but still allows you to maintain the main subject in the left 2/3 of the picture.  Beautiful picture.', '2007-02-12 03:42:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3355759, 461890, 57886, '<td valign="top">Flott mynd, mjög vel gerð... Góð lýsing og myndbygging, flott :o)Ég giska á að hún hefði skorað hærra ef dúkkan hefði verið öll inni á myndinni...? <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-02-12 03:58:08.</i></td>', 'Flott mynd, mjög vel gerð... Góð lýsing og myndbygging, flott :o)Ég giska á að hún hefði skorað hærra ef dúkkan hefði verið öll inni á myndinni...? ', '2007-02-12 03:55:53.000000', '2007-02-12 03:58:08.000000', 0),
(3356054, 456469, 14986, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jr76:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats! I think I know this pond! Is this off of River Road, one of the two ponds across from the wast facility? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yep...that''s the spot!</td>', 'Originally posted by jr76: Congrats! I think I know this pond! Is this off of River Road, one of the two ponds across from the wast facility?   Yep...that''s the spot!', '2007-02-12 06:46:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3356325, 452572, 36606, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by v5planet:</b></div><hr/><i> I am impressed with the warmth of this photo and the quality of the silhouettes. I agree with many others who have commented that it''s hard to get tired of these photos - majestic animals that are incredibly photogenic. <br/> <br/>Only two qualms with the photo: the first is the vertical cropping seems oh-so-slightly harsh. I would''ve liked a deeper vertical dimension. The other complaint is a bit more trivial - the title doesn''t really seem to fit as the two look more like they''re grazing in each other''s proximity than duking it out. <br/> <br/>Altogether a great shot and I look forward to more of your future wildlife photography efforts. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>They certainly were "duking it out" as u put it. I wanted to capture them pretty symetrically, so this is the best timing IMO.<br/> <br/>With regards to the crop - possibly a little too much</td>', 'Originally posted by v5planet: I am impressed with the warmth of this photo and the quality of the silhouettes. I agree with many others who have commented that it''s hard to get tired of these photos - majestic animals that are incredibly photogenic.  Only two qualms with the photo: the first is the vertical cropping seems oh-so-slightly harsh. I would''ve liked a deeper vertical dimension. The other complaint is a bit more trivial - the title doesn''t really seem to fit as the two look more like they''re grazing in each other''s proximity than duking it out.  Altogether a great shot and I look forward to more of your future wildlife photography efforts.   They certainly were "duking it out" as u put it. I wanted to capture them pretty symetrically, so this is the best timing IMO. With regards to the crop - possibly a little too much', '2007-02-12 08:45:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3356368, 461903, 47534, '<td valign="top">Jen,<br/> <br/>I always enjoy your images, and this one is no exception - but the stories you bring to the images... THAT is terrific!  Including your thoughts about the subject is inspirational and makes me want to find my next subject, or learn about a technique you''ve used.<br/> <br/>Thanks for giving us insight into your work!</td>', 'Jen, I always enjoy your images, and this one is no exception - but the stories you bring to the images... THAT is terrific!  Including your thoughts about the subject is inspirational and makes me want to find my next subject, or learn about a technique you''ve used. Thanks for giving us insight into your work!', '2007-02-12 08:57:28.000000', NULL, 0),
