(3366873, 459806, 48389, '<td valign="top">I love the placement of the little girl here, just between the windows with her looking to the light, perfect. I think your editing suits the subject quite nicely and the half smile that is on the young girls face is wonderful. I am not surprised you like this image, very nicely done! :o)</td>', 'I love the placement of the little girl here, just between the windows with her looking to the light, perfect. I think your editing suits the subject quite nicely and the half smile that is on the young girls face is wonderful. I am not surprised you like this image, very nicely done! :o)', '2007-02-14 18:02:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3369851, 456230, 64670, '<td valign="top">Just lovely - I love the mix of snow and sand, really beautiful and something my imagination couldn''t work up.</td>', 'Just lovely - I love the mix of snow and sand, really beautiful and something my imagination couldn''t work up.', '2007-02-15 15:23:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3370153, 460398, 66597, '<td valign="top">Great lines and vanishing point. However, I have to agree with Jeffrey on this one; pretty hard to get a good shot in these conditions without a tripod. I don''t know what the Nikon Coolpix capabilities are, but if the ISO can be turned up to 1600 or even 3200, grain might be better than the slight blur that''s inevitable otherwise sans tripod. I don''t know if the green cast was intentional - if so, please ignore - but if not, maybe consider changing white balance to fluorescent setting or bracket a few shots on different WB settings to see what works best. Finally, I think fill flash might have enhanced the foreground area, depending on how far your flash extends.</td>', 'Great lines and vanishing point. However, I have to agree with Jeffrey on this one; pretty hard to get a good shot in these conditions without a tripod. I don''t know what the Nikon Coolpix capabilities are, but if the ISO can be turned up to 1600 or even 3200, grain might be better than the slight blur that''s inevitable otherwise sans tripod. I don''t know if the green cast was intentional - if so, please ignore - but if not, maybe consider changing white balance to fluorescent setting or bracket a few shots on different WB settings to see what works best. Finally, I think fill flash might have enhanced the foreground area, depending on how far your flash extends.', '2007-02-15 16:31:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3370931, 456868, 66597, '<td valign="top">I really like the simplicity and composition in this photo. I gave it a better than average vote in a difficult challenge for those reasons. I also find the lighting lovely. The only detracting aspect to me is the shadow extending back from the sled, which leads my eye out of the photo.</td>', 'I really like the simplicity and composition in this photo. I gave it a better than average vote in a difficult challenge for those reasons. I also find the lighting lovely. The only detracting aspect to me is the shadow extending back from the sled, which leads my eye out of the photo.', '2007-02-15 20:49:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3371002, 456868, 35669, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by noraneko:</b></div><hr/><i>  The only detracting aspect to me is the shadow extending back from the sled, which leads my eye out of the photo. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was lead out of the frame by the footsteps. awesome.</td>', 'Originally posted by noraneko:  The only detracting aspect to me is the shadow extending back from the sled, which leads my eye out of the photo.   I was lead out of the frame by the footsteps. awesome.', '2007-02-15 21:11:28.000000', NULL, 0),
