(3379931, 460398, 62318, '<td valign="top">I won''t delve too much into the points others made (slight green tint and slight blur) which held the photo back as far as score. What really amazes on this photo, not sure if you did a crop or not, but the lines end almost perfectly at the end of the frames. Amazing the way it was composed (or cropped). Generally, at least what I find appealing, in highly organized shapes and architecture it helps to have the end point not so busy. I think if the hall wasn''t cluttered it would help. I would be tempted to burn it out and see how it fars. Still as I mentioned perfect composition.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-02-19 01:45:00.</i></td>', 'I won''t delve too much into the points others made (slight green tint and slight blur) which held the photo back as far as score. What really amazes on this photo, not sure if you did a crop or not, but the lines end almost perfectly at the end of the frames. Amazing the way it was composed (or cropped). Generally, at least what I find appealing, in highly organized shapes and architecture it helps to have the end point not so busy. I think if the hall wasn''t cluttered it would help. I would be tempted to burn it out and see how it fars. Still as I mentioned perfect composition.', '2007-02-19 01:44:43.000000', '2007-02-19 01:45:00.000000', 0),
